  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far favors multimodal multiprofile PCA with ResNet50, avgpool, and weighted fusion, with config_019 as the current best (accuracy 0.639, F1 0.620). Weighted fusion slightly outperformed concat, and ResNet50 and ViT-L are nearly tied, so the main unresolved choice in this promising family is aggregation: avgpool beat transformer in RNA-only PCA, but it is untested in the best multimodal setting. config_021 changes only aggregation from config_019, isolating whether transformer aggregation can help once image features are fused. This is the best next experiment because it is a clean, single-change extension of the current best direction and will either reveal a better aggregation strategy or confirm avgpool, efficiently reducing uncertainty under a limited budget."
}

